<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The Manipulation tab, against MoveIt's own Manipulation tab
  (motion_planning_rviz_plugin_frame.ui, tab `manipulation`).

  MoveIt's tab is a QGridLayout, two columns:

    row 0, col 0, rowspan 2   Detected Objects    detected_objects_list
                                                 detect_objects_button  &Detect
    row 0, col 1              Support Surfaces    support_surfaces_list
                                                 pick_button            &Pick
                                                 place_button           P&lace
    row 1, col 1              ROI                 "Center (m):" roi_center_x/y/z
                                                 "Size (m):"   roi_size_x/y/z

  WHAT MOVEIT'S MANIPULATION TAB IS
  It is an OBJECT PERCEPTION tab, not a gripper tab. Its three groups are fed
  by moveit_ros_perception: &Detect fires the ObjectRecognition action,
  Support Surfaces is a table/plane detector, and ROI is the region of the
  camera image that recognition is run over. There is no open/close control
  anywhere on it; a ParallelJawGripper is driven from MoveIt's separate
  ACTUATOR panel.

  EVERY CONTROL ON THIS TAB IS ABSENT HERE, AND WHY
  curobo has no perception at all, so all three groups have nothing behind
  them. They are not stubbed: there is no disabled [Detect] that could ever
  turn green, and no ROI spinbox wired to a field that does not exist. What
  remains is MoveIt's frame — the grid, the three group boxes in MoveIt's own
  positions, MoveIt's own titles — and two empty lists, each carrying one
  disabled row that says which service is missing (added from
  manipulation_tab.cpp, so this file stays a transcription).

    &Detect          needs moveit_ros_perception's ObjectRecognition action.
                     curobo publishes no perception action, and has no service
                     that returns a detected object.
    &Pick / P&lace   need a support-surface list, i.e. a table or plane
                     detector. There is no such thing in the service list.
    Center / Size    ROI is the window the recogniser is run over. With no
                     recogniser there is no window, and TrajectoryGoal carries
                     no ROI field, so these would have to be typed for nobody.

  WHAT REPLACED THE GRIPPER TABLE THAT WAS HERE
  This tab used to be MoveIt's Joints table scoped to the gripper joints, with
  Open / Close / Plan / Plan+send on it. That was a misreading of the tab: it
  looked like MoveIt's Joints tab, not its Manipulation tab, and it duplicated
  the Joints tab. Nothing is lost by deleting it — `finger_joint` is in the
  cspace like every other joint, so the Joints tab's table already lists it,
  its bar already spans its own limits, and Plan / Plan + send already plan to
  it. See manipulation_tab.hpp.
-->
